From c9d5a29d447b6f911bdec8b336b57e08ba86a6ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:41:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: a slash command in an agent's code block opens a
 new thread

Agents often end a turn by recommending the next command -- `/epic:epic
stories run 014`, say -- in a code block. The operator then copied it, opened a
new thread and pasted it. A code block in an agent's message that holds one
slash command now carries a second button beside Copy: it opens a new thread
with the same agent and puts the command in that thread's composer (story 020).

**Prefill, never send.** The command goes in through the existing
`AgentInitialContent::ContentBlock { auto_submit: false }` path and waits for
the operator to read it and press Enter. Sending on the operator's behalf was
ruled out: a recommended command can be wrong, stale or for another thread.

**Which blocks qualify.** `slash_command_in_code_block` (crate root) answers by
shape: exactly one non-empty line whose first non-whitespace character is `/`,
trimmed, and not a bare `/`. Two lines, a prompt prefix (`$ /help`) or an
`echo /help` do not. It decides by shape, not by the agent's command list, so a
lone `/usr/bin/foo` qualifies too -- the operator reviews before sending.

**Code blocks only, agent messages only.** Inline code spans are left alone by
choice. The button is drawn by a new markdown hook,
`MarkdownElement::on_code_block_action`, which asks the caller about each code
block and, on `Some`, renders an `IconButton` (`ThreadFromSummary`, tooltip "New
Thread with This Command") before Copy, with Copy's visibility -- shown on
hover with it, absent when Copy is hidden -- and an element id unique per
markdown entity. `crates/markdown` cannot depend on `agent_ui`, hence a hook
like `on_url_click` rather than the policy itself. In `agent_ui` only the
assistant-message branch sets it: `render_message_content` gains
`offers_slash_commands`, false for thinking blocks, which share that path, and
tool output, user messages, compaction errors and the composer preview never
reach it.

**Opening the thread.** `AgentPanel::new_thread_with_prefilled_prompt(agent,
text)` opens it through `external_thread`, focused. The click resolves the
agent with `Agent::from(thread_view.agent_id)`. An agent that is no longer
configured (a custom agent the project's agent-server store does not list --
the same check `create_thread` uses) opens nothing and shows an error toast
naming it, logged at WARN. A successful open logs one INFO line with the agent
id, the source session and the command's length, never its text. The source
thread is left as it was.

Tests: 9 unit tests for the predicate, 6 for the markdown hook (asked with the
block's code, declined blocks, Copy hidden, hover, per-block and per-entity
identity), 3 for the panel method and 4 GPUI tests that sweep the agent panel
for the button and click it (only the qualifying block, not on thinking or
user messages, the trimmed command lands in the new composer unsent).

Pure Zed and generic ACP: it rides `claude-agent-acp-plus` BY CHOICE, like
0014 and 0026, and needs no adapter feature.
---

diff --git a/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs b/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs
